From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom: tsens: skip SM8550 uplow wake IRQ (7.2 adaptation)

7.2 adaptation of Pocknix/ROCKNIX 0203: on SM8550 the ordinary uplow
TSENS IRQ wakes s2idle immediately — pm_wakeup_irq points at it on every
suspend attempt. The 0204 patch in our series already masks the lower
threshold interrupts across suspend; this additionally leaves the uplow
IRQ un-armed as a wakeup source on qcom,sm8550 so it cannot end the
sleep, while critical stays armed. Scoped to the SoC-level compatible.

---
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
@@ -1330,9 +1330,17 @@
 
 	if (priv->feat->combo_int) {
 		enable_irq_wake(priv->combined_irq);
 	} else {
-		enable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
+		/*
+		 * On SM8550 the ordinary uplow IRQ wakes s2idle immediately
+		 * (pm_wakeup_irq points at it on every attempt); leave it as
+		 * non-wakeup. Critical stays armed. (Pocknix/ROCKNIX 0203.)
+		 */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm8550"))
+			enable_irq_wake(priv->uplow_irq);
 		if (priv->feat->crit_int)
 			enable_irq_wake(priv->crit_irq);
 	}
